                      A "Cairnflow Hosting Service" is a service, offered to
                      third parties (anyone other than you, your organization,
                      and your organization's employees and contractors), that
                      lets those third parties reach the Cairnflow APIs in
                      order to register their own deployments or services,
                      invoke them, or create or manage tenants. The
                      "Cairnflow APIs" are every port, protocol and interface
                      exposed by the Licensed Work, including the ingress,
                      administrative, SDK, query and console interfaces.

                      For the avoidance of doubt, the following uses are
                      permitted and are not a Cairnflow Hosting Service:
                       * Running the Licensed Work in production for agents,
                         workflows or services written by you or your
                         organization (including its employees and
                         contractors), including when those serve your own
                         customers.
                       * Running the Licensed Work as an internal platform,
                         including in multi-tenant mode with one tenant per
                         team or business unit, when only you and your
                         organization (including its employees and
                         contractors) can reach the Cairnflow APIs.
                       * Offering a product to third parties that is built on
                         the Licensed Work and exposes its own abstraction
                         (for example a graphical builder, a domain-specific
                         language or a proprietary API), provided that the
                         way those third parties define, add, or start
                         workflows or agents does not use the Cairnflow APIs
                         directly.

                      For the avoidance of doubt, the following uses are not
                      permitted:
                       * A managed service that lets third-party developers
                         register their own deployments or service endpoints
                         and invoke them through that managed service.
                       * Selling or giving third parties tenants, or access
                         to tenants, of an installation of the Licensed Work.

